    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d971">

                <pb facs="1099" n="955" xml:id="pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.05/350: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-19T12:00:00+02:00">November 19,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. My 68, November 14, 4 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d971-f1"/> Am just in
                    receipt of formal note from Minister of Foreign Affairs requesting nominations
                    for Cairo appointment. Shall be asked informally in accordance with practice to
                    indicate which candidate I consider best qualified. Does Department care to
                    instruct me to this end?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
